@meta
id: 03-14
title: Drill — retype the line
chapter: 03
type: drill
skills: insert-ctrl-w
reps: 8
par: 40
minutes: 5
vscode: triple-click, retype
open: standup.md

@brief
Eight times: the Blocked line is out of date and nothing in it is worth
keeping. Get to the end of it, clear it, and type the new one.

`Blocked: waiting on finance` is what it should say.

@keys
| `A` | append at the end of the line |
| `Ctrl-U` | clear the line back to the indent |
| `Esc` | out |

@hints
`A` first. `Ctrl-U` deletes what is before the cursor, so the cursor has
to be at the end for it to take the whole line.
--
`A` `Ctrl-U` is two keys pressed as one movement. Do not look at the line
in between them.

@solution
    A <Ctrl-U> Blocked: waiting on finance <Esc> :wq<Enter>

Thirty-four keystrokes, twenty-seven of them the new line.

Worth noticing as you repeat it: the cost of the edit is now entirely the
typing. There is no selecting, no dragging, no measuring how much to
delete. That is the state you want every small edit to reach, and it is
why the keys in this chapter are worth drilling rather than reading.

`Ctrl-U` respects the indent, so this works exactly the same on a line
buried four levels deep in a class.

@start standup.md
Blocked: nothing

@expected standup.md
Blocked: waiting on finance
